## Multi-Provider LLM Support

The tool now supports multiple LLM backends through a clean provider abstraction:

### Gemini (Cloud)
```bash
LLM_PROVIDER=gemini
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key
LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash    # or gemini-2.0-flash, gemini-1.5-pro
```

Features: context caching (reduces per-iteration cost of the large system prompt), shared token-bucket rate limiter across concurrent agents, server-provided retry delay parsing, automatic cache expiry recreation (up to 3 times before falling back to uncached).

### OpenAI-Compatible (Local or Cloud)
```bash
LLM_PROVIDER=openai-compatible
LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1    # Ollama default
LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5:14b
LLM_CONTEXT_LENGTH=32768                   # Sets num_ctx for Ollama
LLM_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=120000              # Longer timeout for local inference
```

Works with Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio, or any service exposing an OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint. Includes connection error diagnostics ("Is Ollama running?"), JSON repair for malformed tool call arguments, and automatic retries for overloaded model errors.

