## Feature Flag Testing

A dedicated `feature-flags.json` config enables the agent to toggle feature flags during testing and observe their effects:

```json
{
  "provider": "admin-ui",
  "adminUrl": "/admin/feature-flags",
  "flags": [
    {
      "name": "liveStreaming",
      "description": "Enables the live streaming stack (WebRTC broadcasting and viewer page)",
      "defaultState": "off",
      "scope": "tenant",
      "resetAfterTest": true,
      "interactsWith": ["events"]
    }
  ],
  "testingGuidance": "Disabling liveStreaming mid-session after viewing a stream page is a good interaction test."
}
```

The `provider` field controls how flags are toggled: `admin-ui` means the agent navigates to a flag management page within the app (or an external dashboard), while `mcp` routes toggle operations through a dedicated MCP server (e.g. LaunchDarkly). Flag interaction relationships (`interactsWith`) help the agent identify combination tests. The `resetAfterTest` flag ensures the agent cleans up after feature toggle tests.

