## External Systems Cross-Checking

For applications with supporting infrastructure (log aggregators, monitoring dashboards, error trackers), an `external-systems.json` config teaches the agent to verify test actions against external evidence:

```json
{
  "systems": [
    {
      "name": "Kibana",
      "purpose": "Application logs, error tracking, and audit trail verification",
      "url": "http://localhost:5601",
      "credentials": { "identifierType": "username", "identifier": "elastic", "password": "changeme" },
      "checkAfter": ["error responses (4xx/5xx)", "failed login attempts", "data mutations"],
      "searchGuidance": "Use the Discover view with the app-* index pattern. Filter by @timestamp within the last 5 minutes."
    }
  ],
  "checkRoles": ["platform admin", "tenant admin"],
  "generalGuidance": "After any write operation, a corresponding audit log entry should exist in Kibana within seconds."
}
```

This enables a testing pattern that human testers use instinctively but that's hard to automate: performing an action in the app, then checking the logs to see if the right things were recorded. The `checkRoles` setting prevents low-privilege roles from wasting iterations on systems they can't access.

