## Configurability: Everything Is Tuneable

The `settings.json` for each app profile controls every aspect of behaviour:

| Setting | Purpose | Default |
|---------|---------|---------|
| `browser.engine` | Browser engine (chromium, firefox, webkit) | `chromium` |
| `browser.headless` | Run without visible browser window | `false` |
| `browser.launchArgs` | Chrome flags (disable password prompts, etc.) | see defaults |
| `agent.maxResultChars` | Max characters kept per tool result | `8000` |
| `agent.contextWindowSize` | Recent entries kept during compression | `20` |
| `agent.contextSummaryThreshold` | History length that triggers compression | `40` |
| `agent.minToolCallsBeforeComplete` | Minimum browser interactions before completion | `15` |
| `agent.maxDismissAttempts` | Max blocker dismiss retries per encounter | `6` |
| `context.maxAppContextChars` | Truncation limit for app context | `12000` |
| `context.maxHistoricalBugsChars` | Truncation limit for historical bugs | `10000` |
| `context.contextPriority` | Section ordering for context window truncation | see defaults |
| `issueTracker.enabled` | Enable the issue filing subsystem (when `false`, no issue processing occurs at all) | `false` |
| `issueTracker.dedupeByTitle` | Skip filing if an open issue with same title exists | `true` |
| `issueTracker.dryRun` | When `enabled` is `true`: extract and log findings but don't actually call GitHub APIs — preview what *would* be filed | `false` |
| `pricing.inputPer1M` / `outputPer1M` | Token cost rates for cost estimation | Gemini Flash rates |
| `mcpServers` | Additional MCP server configs (feature flags, etc.) | `[]` |

Environment variables override everything. `PLAYWRIGHT_HEADLESS=true` for CI runs. `VERBOSE=true` for debugging. `LLM_PROVIDER=openai-compatible` to switch LLM backends. Per-role `maxIterations` and `model` overrides let you allocate more budget and a more capable model to complex roles.

